Calculation:

Let h₁ and h₂ be the height of triangles ABC and PQR and b₁ and b₂ be the base of triangles ABC and PQR

Given

h₁ = 5 and h₂ = 3

frac{{Area of triangle ABC}}{{Area of triangle PQR}} = ({frac{1)/(2) base times height}}{{(1)/(2)base times height}}

Rightarrow (4)/(5) = ({frac{1)/(2) times {b₁} times {h₁}}}{{(1)/(2) times {b₂} times {h₂}}}

Rightarrow (4)/(5) = frac{{{b₁} times 5}}{{{b₂} times 3}}

therefore frac{{{b₁}}}{{{b₂}}} = frac{{12}}{{25}}
